now let's try finding the square root of  11,000 25 using the prime factorization  method hence our aim would be to reduce  11,000 25 into its prime factors so we  write 11,000 25 here and draw 2 lines  like this if we know the rules of  divisibility well we can say that this  number is divisible by 3 5 and 7 so we  can start with any prime number say 5 so  5 x 2,205 gives us 11,000 25 this number  again is divisible by 5  hence we write a 5 here and 5 multiplied  by 441 gives us 2,205 of course you  would take a bit more time to find the  numbers here but that's perfectly  alright and remember we keep just the  prime factors on the left hand side now  since 441 is divisible by 3 let us write  3 here and 3 x 147 gives us 441 this  number is also divisible by 3 and 3 x 49  equals 147 and the only prime number 49  is divisible by is 7 and 7 multiplied by  7 is 49 and yes we stopped here since 7  is a prime number so 11,000 25 can be  written as 5 times 5 times 3 times 3  times 7 times 7  hence the square root of 11,000 25 can  be written as square root of 5 times 5  times 3 times 3 times 7 times 7 the next  step is to make pairs of the same  numbers and after we find the pair's  we choose one number from each pair so  we have three pairs here a pair of 5s a  pair of threes and a pair of 7s we  choose one number from each pair so from  the first pair  we choose five from the second pair we  choose three and from the third pair we  choose a seven and to find the square  root all we have to do is multiply these  numbers 5 x 3 x 7 equals 105 hence the  square root of 11,000 25 is 105 this  part of the problem where we choose one  number from each pair is really simple  what we really need to be good at is  finding out the prime factors quickly  here's another interesting thing you  need to know finding the prime factors  of large numbers can be difficult and  tedious so yes there is a better way to  find them which we will see in the  coming videos  you
 

